          "id": "b01",
          "text": "Let's solve this one step by step. Three plus four times the quantity two minus five, squared.",
          "display": "3 + 4 × (2 − 5)^2",
          "cue": "show-problem",
          "pause_after_s": 1.2
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s02",
      "title": "Step by step",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "b02",
          "text": "Parentheses first. Two minus five is negative three.",
          "display": "3 + 4 × (−3)^2",
          "cue": "step-1"
        },
        {
          "id": "b03",
          "text": "Now the exponent. Negative three squared is nine.",
          "display": "3 + 4 × 9",
          "cue": "step-2"
        },
        {
          "id": "b04",
          "text": "Then multiplication. Four times nine is thirty-six.",
          "display": "3 + 36",
          "cue": "step-3"
        },
        {
          "id": "b05",
          "text": "Last, three plus thirty-six is thirty-nine.",
          "display": "39",
          "cue": "step-4"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s03",
      "title": "The answer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "b06",
          "text": "So the answer is thirty-nine.",
          "display": "= 39",
          "cue": "answer"
        },
        {
          "id": "b07",
          "text": "Watch out for these traps. If you add three plus four first, you get sixty-three. If you square only the five, you get negative eighty-nine.",
          "cue": "traps"
        }
      ]
